    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4887da31_d7b6f53d",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 19,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002790
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-24T11:38:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "An entry carries a Name and a Board and the object is closed to anything else, so it can only name a device, not describe one. What the device is stays in the configuration of the board it is on, which exposes a record for it, and the Name here has to match that record\u0027s InventoryName for the two to be paired [1].\n\nThe wording is mine to fix though: \"somewhere to put per device properties later\" does read as describing the downstream device, which is not what the closed object allows. I will drop that clause and keep the reason that survives: an entry can gain its own BridgedEndpoints if a bridged device is itself a bridge.\n\n[1] https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/entity-manager/+/93517",
      "parentUuid": "5fb04993_0c599d7f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 18,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 19,
        "endChar": 16
      },
      "revId": "9215f32088ed58f2100c004b43ae10214d35043b",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
