      "writtenOn": "2026-08-24T07:39:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why do we know this? And how do we name it in the event that the board name is dynamic based on e.g. `$bus` for that board (I can\u0027t see why we can assume it is the same as `$bus` for _this_ board).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 7,
        "startChar": 36,
        "endLine": 7,
        "endChar": 89
      },
      "revId": "9215f32088ed58f2100c004b43ae10214d35043b",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a8efc6d6_3df3e974",
        "filename": "schemas/platform/mctp.json",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 7,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002790
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-24T11:38:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The platform does not assume the name, it requires it: the Probe carries a FOUND precondition for each board a record references, so a name that does not resolve stops the platform configuration from applying rather than pairing a device with the wrong board.\n\nA templated reference would not work, as you say: a $bus written here resolves against the platform\u0027s own probe, not the referenced board\u0027s. So a record names a board by the name that board resolves to, and FOUND is what checks the two agree.\n\nYou have also caught something that is not about this patch: the GPU board templates on $index, which is the order the FRUs were matched in rather than where the board sits.",
      "parentUuid": "17b22526_fbfd0d20",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 7,
        "startChar": 36,
        "endLine": 7,
        "endChar": 89
      },
